import ../../site/actions.dl
import site_fixture.dl
import ../../site/packages/dynlex-ui/testing/driver.dl

the site's pages means: [home page, IDE page]

to [paint Farm label test] {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    set state to the website state in (painting's instance)
    set state's farm's viewport to painting's bounds
    resize website Farm camera (the address of (state's farm's renderer's camera)) to (painting's bounds)
    project website Farm names in state

to [paint empty label test] {a pointer to UI canvas frame:painting}:
    ignore painting

to [press Farm label test at] {UI point:point} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view

to [release Farm label test at] {UI point:point} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at (point's x) (point's y) with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    ignore update UI view view

to get [the Farm label test center of] {a pointer to UI floating control:name}:
    set box to name's layout's hit bounds
    require condition ((box's width > 0.0) and (box's height > 0.0)) reporting "The test label is not visible"
    return a UI point at (box's x + box's width * 0.5) and (box's y + box's height * 0.5)

to get [a Farm label test destination for] {a pointer to website farm actor:actor} [in] {a pointer to website state:state}:
    set world to state's farm's document's world
    set name to the website Farm name for (actor's id) in (state's farm's names)
    set origin to the Farm label test center of name
    loop y from (actor's y - 2) to (actor's y + 3):
        loop x from (actor's x - 2) to (actor's x + 3):
            if (x != actor's x) or (y != actor's y):
                if website farm land at x y is walkable in world except actor actor:
                    set point to the website Farm scene point at x y in world
                    set projection to the UI scene projection for point through (state's farm's renderer's camera's orbit's camera) in (state's farm's viewport)
                    if projection's visible:
                        set dx to projection's screen's x - origin's x
                        set dy to projection's screen's y - origin's y
                        # Move far enough to exercise a drag instead of a click.
                        if ((dx * dx) + (dy * dy)) >= 144.0:
                            return website farm point x y
    require condition false reporting "The Farm label test has no visible free drop square"
    return a new website farm point

set instance to an instance of website fixture
show page "/index.html" in (the address of instance)
set driver to the value at the test UI driver
set driver's shader operations to the browser UI shader operations
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 1600 by 1100 using font "regular" with (the address of driver)
set state to a new website state
set state's services to the browser UI service provider
set state's view to the address of view
set state's route to "/index.html"
set instance's state to (the address of state) as a pointer
set state's farm's names to UI floating controls attached to (the control labeled "Farm scene" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of view)
open website source editors in (the address of state)
initialize the website Farm in (the address of state)
open website Farm document in (the address of state)
set session to the address of (state's farm)
set session's renderer to a website Farm renderer for (session's document's world) in (UI box at 0 0 sized 600 450) using shader (42 as a pointer) in (the address of view)
set the value of "Challenge views" in (the address of instance) to 2
bind (the control labeled "Live shader" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "paint empty label test $") for event 1
bind (the control labeled "River scene" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "paint empty label test $") for event 1
bind (the control labeled "Farm scene" in (the address of instance)) in (the address of instance) to (the function named "paint Farm label test $") for event 1
watch UI input in (the address of view) using (the function named "read website Farm input $")
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set canvas to the UI layout labeled "Farm scene" in (view's layout)
set top to the top of canvas inside (view's layout) below 0.0
set view's layout's scroll target and view's layout's scroll position to top
request a UI redraw in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set names to session's names
set document to session's document
set world to document's world
set count to 0
set name to names's first
loop while name != (0 as a pointer to UI floating control):
    increment count
    set name to name's next
require condition (count = (the length of world's workers) + 1) reporting "Farm labels did not include every person"
set player to the website Farm name for (world's player's id) in names
set actor to the item at 0 in (world's workers)
set worker to the website Farm name for (actor's id) in names
set point to the Farm label test center of worker
press Farm label test at point in (the address of view)
release Farm label test at point in (the address of view)
require condition (document's selected = actor's id) reporting "A worker name click did not select that person"
set point to the Farm label test center of player
press Farm label test at point in (the address of view)
release Farm label test at point in (the address of view)
require condition ((document's selected = "player") and (world's player's target's present = false)) reporting "A name click also clicked the terrain below it"
set identity to the address of (worker's node)
set actor's name to "Ada 🌻"
refresh website Farm controls in (the address of state)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (((the UI value for identity in (the address of instance))'s text = "Ada 🌻") and (identity = (the address of (worker's node)))) reporting "Renaming a person replaced the retained label or lost Unicode"
set destination to a Farm label test destination for actor in (the address of state)
set position to the website Farm scene point at (destination's x) (destination's y) in world
set projection to the UI scene projection for position through (session's renderer's camera's orbit's camera) in (session's viewport)
press Farm label test at (the Farm label test center of worker) in (the address of view)
release Farm label test at (projection's screen) in (the address of view)
require condition ((actor's x = destination's x) and (actor's y = destination's y)) reporting "Dragging a name did not use the existing worker placement gesture"
require condition ((actor's held = false) and ((session's pointer name = false) and (session's pointer mode = 0))) reporting "A completed name drag retained pointer capture"
require condition ((document's selected = actor's id) and (world's player's target's present = false)) reporting "A worker name drag also activated a terrain or button click"
set id to formatted "worker-{the next website farm entity in world}"
set spawn to a Farm label test destination for (world's player) in (the address of state)
append (a website farm worker named "New person" identified by id at (spawn's x) (spawn's y)) to world's workers
update website Farm world view in (the address of state) instantly true
require condition ((the website Farm name for id in names) != (0 as a pointer to UI floating control)) reporting "A new worker did not receive a retained label"
reload website Farm progress in (the address of state)
require condition ((the website Farm name for id in names) = (0 as a pointer to UI floating control)) reporting "Replacing the saved world retained a removed person's label"
leave website Farm in (the address of state)
set name to names's first
loop while name != (0 as a pointer to UI floating control):
    require condition (name's visible = false) reporting "Leaving Farm retained an interactive scene label"
    set name to name's next
close website Farm in (the address of state)
free UI source workspace (state's language)
close the address of view
close the address of instance
set pending to state's requests
loop while pending != (0 as a pointer to website request):
    set next to pending's next
    deallocate pending
    set pending to next
print line "Farm names retain identity through selection, Unicode renaming, dragging, new people, profile replacement and scene lifetime."
